@startuml
title Selected Architecture 1 - Atomic Payment Settlement
start
:Authenticate debtor and display authorized balance;
:Enter group, payee, currency, amount,
payment date and stable request ID;
:Begin transaction;
note right
  SQLite: BEGIN IMMEDIATE before reads.
  PostgreSQL: READ COMMITTED;
  shared group access guard first.
end note
:Recheck current membership and actor/debtor identity;
if (Authorized?) then (yes)
  :Reserve or load scoped OperationReceipt;
else (no)
  :Roll back; deny access;
  stop
endif
if (Accepted receipt exists?) then (yes)
  if (Request hash matches?) then (yes)
    :End transaction; return original payment result;
  else (no)
    :Roll back; return idempotency conflict;
  endif
  stop
endif
:Acquire stable directional debt-pair guard
in PostgreSQL; SQLite write lock already held;
:Calculate latest debt from committed
approved postings minus payment offsets;
:Validate distinct accounts, currency,
positive amount, date and precision;
if (Valid and amount <= latest outstanding?) then (yes)
  :Insert immutable Payment exactly once;
  :Append unique payment offset posting;
  :Save accepted OperationReceipt;
  :Commit payment, posting and receipt together;
  :Return payment ID and committed financial result;
else (no)
  :Roll back; return actionable error;
  :Leave payment history and ledger unchanged;
endif
stop
@enduml
